00:00:20.223 --> 00:00:34.072
Is it a) 33, b) 339, or c) 3,398?

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:42.962
<v><b>Assistant:</b></v> The answer is… 3,398.

00:00:43.775 --> 00:00:53.438
There were 3,398 US episodes of the TV quiz show <i>Who Wants to Be a Millionaire?</i>

00:00:54.447 --> 00:01:00.666
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Question 2. How many places in the US have a quiz night?

00:01:01.297 --> 00:01:11.909
Is it about a) 100, b) 1,000, or c) 10,000?

00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:18.649
<v><b>Assistant:</b></v> The answer is… 10,000.

00:01:19.102 --> 00:01:24.183
About 10,000 places have a quiz night in the US.

00:01:25.138 --> 00:01:33.815
<v><b>Host:</b></v> Question 3. What is the most money that somebody won on a TV quiz show in the US?

00:01:34.607 --> 00:01:59.309
Is it a) 2,520,700 dollars, b) 12,520,700 dollars, or c) 22,520,700 dollars?

00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:10.703
<v><b>Assistant:</b></v> The answer is… 2,520,700 dollars.

00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:23.832
The most money that somebody won on a TV quiz show in the US is 2,520,700 dollars.